================================================================================
Vulnerability data
================================================================================

OtterSight does not redistribute these datasets; it queries or downloads them
at scan time and shows the results. Terms of the respective source apply.

ENISA EU Vulnerability Database (EUVD) — https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/
  Vulnerability data: ENISA EU Vulnerability Database (EUVD), source
  acknowledged. Reproduction authorised provided the source is acknowledged.
  OtterSight is not affiliated with or endorsed by ENISA.

Anchore Grype vulnerability database — https://github.com/anchore/grype-db
  Built by Anchore from upstream sources including the NVD, the GitHub
  Advisory Database and Linux distribution feeds; the upstream terms apply.
  grype-db tooling is licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

GitHub Advisory Database — https://github.com/github/advisory-database
  Licensed under CC-BY-4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
  Received via the Grype database and OSV.dev.

National Vulnerability Database (NVD) — https://nvd.nist.gov/
  Received via the Grype database. This product uses data from the NVD but
  is not endorsed or certified by the NVD.

CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog
  https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog
  Released under CC0 1.0. Received via EUVD's KEV data, with the
  cisagov/kev-data GitHub mirror as fallback.

Exploit Prediction Scoring System (EPSS) — https://www.first.org/epss/
  EPSS scores by FIRST, received via the Grype database.

OSV.dev — https://osv.dev/
  Operated by Google. Used for CVE aliases of GHSA-only findings (disable with
  --no-osv). Data is subject to the terms of each upstream source.
